WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.139
<v NARRATOR>Priya's been quiet all through dinner.

00:00:02.139 --> 00:00:02.814
<v NARRATOR>Shaky, even.

00:00:02.814 --> 00:00:03.658
<v NARRATOR>Maya's noticed.

00:00:03.658 --> 00:00:08.892
<v NARRATOR>Meanwhile, in the group chat, the sophomores are already planning the next late-night lineup.

00:00:08.892 --> 00:00:12.606
<v NARRATOR>Maya doesn't want to blow things up or get Priya labeled a snitch.

00:00:12.606 --> 00:00:16.884
<v NARRATOR>But she also doesn't want to just wait and hope Priya feels better tomorrow.

00:00:16.884 --> 00:00:19.923
<v NARRATOR>So what does she actually do with her phone right now?

00:00:19.923 --> 00:00:24.594
<v NARRATOR>Start with the question that decides everything else: is Priya in danger right now?

00:00:24.594 --> 00:00:31.854
<v NARRATOR>If someone is unconscious, having trouble breathing, or showing signs of alcohol poisoning, none of the other options come first.

00:00:31.854 --> 00:00:34.893
<v NARRATOR>You call 911 or campus emergency services immediately.

00:00:34.893 --> 00:00:42.378
<v NARRATOR>That's not one choice among several — it's the one that overrides every other channel the moment someone is in that kind of distress.
